      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "title": "Support Animation on Canvas Views",
        "action": "Extend the canvas view renderer so a declarative canvas payload can describe time-based animation as well as static shapes. Preserve the existing canvas view contract while adding a safe animation loop and an animation vocabulary suitable for effects such as proton quiver, electron sparks or arcs, pulsing, flicker, and other procedural motion.",
        "expectedEvidence": "A canvas-backed view can animate continuously from graph-authored data without embedding executable code in the graph. Static canvas views continue to render unchanged, animation starts and stops with the view lifecycle, and the chemistry particle views can use the same declarative canvas surface for both still and animated presentation.",
        "status": "todo",
        "definitionKey": "idea-next-step",
        "_classBinding": {
          "key": "idea-next-step",
